+/*
+ * ESP32-S3 GPIO, GPIO matrix and IO_MUX
+ *
+ * The pins are wires: named GPIO lines let boards and tests connect devices to them.
+ *   "pin-in"  [49] in:  a level driven onto the pin from outside (0 or 1); any other
+ *                       value releases it, and the chip or the pull resistors decide
+ *   "pin-out" [49] out: the pin's level, each time it changes
+ *   "sig-out" [256] in: peripheral output signals, routed to pins by the GPIO matrix
+ *                       (FUNC_OUT_SEL_CFG)
